---
// DRAFT privacy policy (English version of /privacidade). Review before going live.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../config';
---
<Base lang="en" route="privacy" title="Privacy policy" description="How VirtusPromPT handles the personal data collected on this website.">
  <section class="page"><div class="wrap">
    <p class="mono eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="mono updated">Last updated: November 2026</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Who is responsible for your data</h2>
      <p>{SITE.legalName} ({SITE.brand}), based in Portugal. For any question about your data, write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>

      <h2>What data we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The details you send through the contact form: name, company (optional), email, reason for contact and message.</li>
        <li>If you book a meeting, the details you enter on Calendly.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We don’t use advertising or tracking cookies. The site only stores your light or dark mode preference, in your own browser.</p>

      <h2>What we use it for</h2>
      <p>Only to reply to your message, prepare proposals and manage any business relationship that follows. The legal basis is your request and the pre-contractual steps it involves.</p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>We don’t sell or hand over your data. We use service providers that process it on our behalf:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Netlify (website hosting and form handling);</li>
        <li>Google Workspace (email);</li>
        <li>Calendly (meeting scheduling, if you use it).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Some of these providers may process data outside the European Union, with the safeguards required by the GDPR, such as standard contractual clauses.</p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>We keep contact details for up to 12 months after the last communication, unless a contract follows, in which case the legal retention periods apply.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask to access, correct, delete, restrict or port your data, or object to its processing, by writing to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. You can also complain to the Portuguese data protection authority, CNPD (<a href="https://www.cnpd.pt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cnpd.pt</a>).</p>
    </div>
  </div></section>
</Base>
